From 0ed8fed422126685bdb5f80e290dd4cc12005f71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zack Maril <zmaril@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:49:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Load early metadata, and swap in full metadata before
 codegen

With `-Zearly-metadata`, a crate can be compiled against a dependency's
early metadata while that dependency is still checking its bodies:

- The locator also considers `libfoo-hash.early-rmeta`, for `--extern`
  and when searching directories, and loads the full metadata instead if
  it exists. Writing early metadata deletes stale full metadata, so a full
  file next to early metadata is never older. A crate that links, given a
  dependency's metadata, records the rlib next to it if the dependency is
  still compiling (it holds the rlib's lock) or the rlib is already there;
  otherwise a missing rlib is reported as before.
- Before code generation, `CStore::load_full_metadata` replaces every
  dependency loaded from early metadata with its full metadata, checking
  the crate hash. The early `CrateMetadata` stays alive, so whatever was
  decoded from it stays valid; lookups return the full one from then on.
  Types cached by their position in the early blob are dropped, and source
  files are imported again from the full blob. Before linking (or, with
  cross-crate LTO, before code generation), `CStore::wait_for_rlibs` waits
  for the rlibs.
- Waiting: if a file isn't written yet, the compilation announces a
  `wait-metadata` artifact notification naming it, and waits for the lock
  its producer holds until it's written; then it announces `resume`. A
  build tool can give its job slot to other work meanwhile. If the lock is
  released and the file isn't there, the dependency failed or crashed, and
  the compilation stops with an error.

None of this runs without the flag.

The run-make test builds a crate from early metadata with the full
metadata hidden and its lock held, at `opt-level` 0 and 2, and checks that
the program is the same as one built from full metadata; and that the
crate stops with an error if the lock is released without the full
metadata.

